{
  "about": "GENERATED — do not hand-edit `durations`, `tests`, `source` or `partitions`. Run: pnpm run e2e:partitions:generate --from <results.json> --as <label>. Only `about`, `why` and `measuredFrom` are prose, and `pnpm run e2e:partitions:check` guards the rest.",
  "why": "HARDEN-04 / DEBT-128, corrected by HARDEN-06A (F-03). Playwright --shard divides the suite by test COUNT; these seconds are what each spec file actually COSTS, and the partitions below are balanced on them. Every spec file the gate runs MUST appear in `durations`, `tests` and `source` — `check` fails while any is sized by the `defaultSpecSeconds` guess, because a guess is not evidence and ten of them are what made partition p05 of run 32321840125 exceed globalTimeout with 33 tests never executed.",
  "measuredFrom": [
    "HARDEN-06A, 2026-08-20. Every one of the 111 spec files is measured, and every one of them from THE SAME RUN — the first time that has been true.",
    "GitHub Actions run 32333645709 (ubuntu-24.04, workers: 1), the twelve-partition gate on the HARDEN-06A branch. All twelve partitions published an e2e-results-<partition> artifact, green ones included, which is the mechanism DEBT-157 was raised for; `generate --from` was then re-run over the complete set of twelve. 1847 tests collected, 1847 executed, none left unexecuted.",
    "The two shards of e2e/responsive.spec.ts (p11, p12) are added together rather than overwriting one another — the reports hold different tests of one file. It measures 1416.6 s over 519 tests, against the 1141.7 s / 465 tests the manifest had carried since HARDEN-04.",
    "What this replaced: ten spec files sized at the 120 s defaultSpecSeconds guess (tasks-dependencies really costs 335 s), and the interim local measurements HARDEN-06A used to get a finishing run in the first place. As of HARDEN-06A no local, normalised or extrapolated figure survived in this file; HARDEN-06B added exactly one and says so in the note below (a NEW spec file cannot have a CI measurement before the run that first executes it). Nothing here is normalised or extrapolated either way.",
    "Refresh it the same way: download a run's e2e-results-* artifacts and run pnpm run e2e:partitions:generate --from <each results.json> --as ci:<run id>. pnpm run e2e:partitions:check fails if any spec file on disk is left without a duration, a test count or a source.",
    "HARDEN-06B, 2026-08-20. ONE file carries a LOCAL measurement: e2e/meetings-concurrency.spec.ts, the two-writer Meeting journey F-01's repair required, measured at 38.0 s over 3 tests on this sandbox (source `local:harden-06b`). It is stated rather than smuggled in: every other figure in this file still comes from CI run 32333645709, and this one should be replaced from the first CI run that publishes an e2e-results artefact including it. The sandbox measured e2e/meetings-follow-up.spec.ts at 78 s against the manifest's 72.3 s, so the local figure is close to CI scale rather than normalised from it.",
    "DHDS-09, 2026-08-21. ONE more file carries a LOCAL measurement: e2e/floating-surfaces.spec.ts, the floating-surface journeys this phase adds, measured at 51.6 s over 8 tests on this sandbox (source `local:dhds-09`). Stated for the same reason HARDEN-06B stated its own: a new spec file has no CI figure to take, and a spec sized at the 120 s default guess would be sized by a guess. Replace it from the first CI run that publishes an e2e-results artefact including it."
  ],
